```

### Game UI

Build your own runtime UI:

```text
Canvas
Panel
Button
Text
Image
ProgressBar
```

---

# PHASE 16 — Scripting

Now allow game developers to write gameplay separately from engine code.

```text
C++ Engine
      │
      ▼
Scripting API
      │
      ▼
Lua
```

Example:

```lua
function Player:update(dt)

    if input:is_pressed("Jump") then
        self:jump()
    end

end
```

Expose:

```text
Entity
Transform
Input
Audio
Physics
Animation
UI
```

---

# PHASE 17 — Editor

Only now build your serious editor.

```text
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ File  Edit  View  Game  Build                     │
├────────────┬──────────────────────┬───────────────┤
│ Hierarchy  │                      │ Inspector     │
│            │                      │               │
│ Player     │       Scene          │ Transform     │
│ Enemy      │       View           │ Mesh          │
│ Camera     │                      │ Material      │
│ Light      │                      │ Physics       │
│            │                      │               │
├────────────┴──────────────────────┴───────────────┤
│ Console │ Assets │ Profiler │ Debug               │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Editor features:

```text
Scene Editor
Hierarchy
Inspector
Asset Browser
Material Editor
Shader Editor
Animation Editor
Console
Profiler
```

---

# PHASE 18 — Job System

Now optimize CPU work.

```text
Main Thread
     │
     ▼
Job System
 ┌───┼────┬────┐
 ▼   ▼    ▼    ▼
Job Job  Job  Job
```

Example:

```text
Frame
 │
 ├── Animation Job
 ├── Physics Job
 ├── AI Job
 ├── Visibility Job
 └── Asset Job
```

Use:

```text
std::thread
std::atomic
std::condition_variable
```

Then build your own worker pool/task graph.

---

# PHASE 19 — Profiler

You cannot optimize what you cannot measure.

Track:

```text
CPU Frame Time
GPU Frame Time
Draw Calls
Memory
Allocations
Entity Count
Physics Time
Animation Time
AI Time
```

Use:

**Tracy**

and:

**RenderDoc**

Architecture:

```text
Engine
 ↓
Profiler
 ├── CPU
 ├── GPU
 ├── Memory
 └── Rendering
```

---

# PHASE 20 — Networking

Only after the single-player engine works.

```text
Client
  │
  │ UDP
  ▼
Server
```

Implement:

```text
Connection
Packet
Serialization
Replication
Server Authority
Client Prediction
Interpolation
Lag Compensation
```

Start with a tiny multiplayer prototype.

