# 🧠 The Most Important Architecture

Eventually you want:

```text
                     GAME
                      │
                      ▼
               ┌─────────────┐
               │   Gameplay  │
               └──────┬──────┘
                      │
                      ▼
                 ENGINE API
                      │
       ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
       ▼              ▼              ▼
      ECS          Systems         Assets
       │              │              │
       └──────────────┼──────────────┘
                      ▼
                 ENGINE CORE
                      │
        ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
        ▼             ▼             ▼
      Memory       Threading       Math
        │             │             │
        └─────────────┼─────────────┘
                      ▼
                 PLATFORM
                      │
            ┌─────────┼─────────┐
            ▼         ▼         ▼
          SDL3      OS API    Filesystem
                      │
                      ▼
                 HARDWARE
```

# 🗺️ Your First 12 Months

Don't try to finish everything immediately.

| Month | Goal                       |
| ----- | -------------------------- |
| 1     | C++ + CMake + SDL3         |
| 2     | Game loop + Input + Math   |
| 3     | 2D Renderer                |
| 4     | ECS                        |
| 5     | Asset + Scene System       |
| 6     | 3D Renderer                |
| 7     | Physics + Audio            |
| 8     | Animation + AI             |
| 9     | UI + Scripting             |
| 10    | Editor                     |
| 11    | Profiling + Multithreading |
| 12    | Multiplayer + Packaging    |

## 🎯 First game milestone

Don't aim for "build Unreal Engine."

Aim for this:

```text
             YOUR ENGINE

        ┌──────────────────┐
        │      Player      │
        │        🧍        │
        │                  │
        │   🧱       👾    │
        │                  │
        │       🏁         │
        └──────────────────┘

        ↓
      Input
        ↓
      ECS
        ↓
    Physics
        ↓
    Renderer
        ↓
      Audio
```

Build a **small 2D platformer** with your engine first. Once that works end-to-end, move to 3D. That single decision will dramatically reduce the complexity of the project while giving you a complete engine architecture to evolve.
